# Development Rules

## Core Philosophy
- **Stack**: Next.js (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion. 
- **Style Overrides**: Use Tailwind utility classes (`className="flex flex-col gap-4..."`) combined with CSS Variables for semantic theming (`var(--surface-ground)`).
- **Reconciled Instructions**: Ignore legacy instructions restricting `<div>` usage or Tailwind classes. Tailwind and standard HTML/JSX semantics are the active styling engine.

## Component & Layout Rules
- **Structure**: Use semantic HTML (`<section>`, `<article>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`) and structural `<div>` elements. 
- **Spacing**: Use standard Tailwind spacing scales (`py-24`, `gap-8`, `mb-16`).
- **Typography**: Adhere to the established font families via Tailwind classes (`font-mono`, `font-serif`, `font-sans`).

## Design & Accessibility
- **Motion**: Use Framer Motion (`<motion.div>`) strictly for `transform` and `opacity` properties. Always wrap animations in `prefers-reduced-motion` checks or use the `shouldReduceMotion` hook.
- **Accessibility**: Ensure all interactive elements (buttons, links) have `focus-visible:ring-2` focus states and proper `aria-labels` for icons.

## Anti-Patterns
- NO inline styles unless dynamically calculated by Framer Motion.
- NO arbitrary UI libraries or generic template components without explicit permission.
- NO layout-shifting animations (`transition-all` on padding/margins).
